  "tagline": "IBM's FPGA-accelerated MPP warehouse, now offered as NPS on-prem, in Cloud Pak and as a service.",
  "description": "Netezza pioneered the data warehouse appliance in the early 2000s, pairing commodity CPUs with FPGAs that filter and decompress data as it streams off disk. IBM acquired it in 2010 and, after briefly sunsetting the appliance, revived it as Netezza Performance Server: on the new Barracuda appliance, on Cloud Pak for Data System, and as a managed service on AWS, Azure and IBM Cloud. The 11.3 line moves to RHEL 8 and adds Iceberg integration with watsonx.data. It suits long-time Netezza shops that want continuity; everyone else usually picks a cloud-native warehouse.",
